{
  "summary": "Optimizes four per-transaction validation steps across transaction check and block connection. It replaces `std::set` in `CheckTransaction` with a pairwise scan for transactions with up to 96 inputs (and `std::sort` for larger ones), bypasses previous block median time past calculation in `EvaluateSequenceLocks` when no time-based relative lock applies, skips coin lookups for sequence locks in `ConnectBlock` when BIP68 is not enforced or not active on a transaction, and combines P2SH and witness sigop counting passes in `GetTransactionSigOpCost` to avoid duplicate coin cache lookups.",
  "problem": "Block connection and transaction validation perform redundant work on every transaction, including heap allocations for duplicate-input sets, median-time-past chain walks for transactions without relative locktimes, coin lookups for relative lock heights when locks are disabled or unenforced, and duplicate coin cache lookups when calculating sigop costs.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author microbenchmarks duplicate input checks on an 8-core machine showing a 1.26x to 3.13x speedup for 1 to 96 inputs (e.g., 248.71 ns reduced to 79.39 ns at 16 inputs).",
    "Author reindex benchmark (`bitcoind --reindex-chainstate` to block 974,000 on a 6-core machine) reports a completion time reduction from 4h 14m 25s down to 4h 11m 58s (a speedup of 2 minutes 27 seconds, or roughly 1%)."
