  "card": "Optimizes four per-transaction validation checks during block connection and transaction verification: replaces the std::set duplicate-input check with a pairwise scan for small transactions and std::sort for large ones, avoids median-time-past calculation when no time-based sequence lock applies, skips sequence-lock coin lookups when BIP68 is not enforced or active, and merges P2SH and witness sigop counting loops. The author reports a 1.2x to 3.1x microbenchmark speedup on duplicate-input checks and a 2.5-minute (~1%) reduction during chainstate reindex up to block 974,000. All four optimizations touch consensus-critical validation paths.",
